# LLM Providers (set the one you use)
OPENAI_API_KEY=
GOOGLE_API_KEY=
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
XAI_API_KEY=
DEEPSEEK_API_KEY=
DASHSCOPE_API_KEY=
DASHSCOPE_CN_API_KEY=
ZHIPU_API_KEY=
ZHIPU_CN_API_KEY=
MINIMAX_API_KEY=
MINIMAX_CN_API_KEY=
OPENROUTER_API_KEY=
MISTRAL_API_KEY=
MOONSHOT_API_KEY=
GROQ_API_KEY=
NVIDIA_API_KEY=

# FRED (Federal Reserve macro data: rates, inflation, labor, growth). Free key: https://fred.stlouisfed.org/docs/api/api_key.html
#FRED_API_KEY=

# Optional: a custom OpenAI-compatible endpoint (vLLM, LM Studio, llama.cpp,
# relay). Select provider "openai_compatible" and set the base URL; the key is
# optional (local servers need none).
#OPENAI_COMPATIBLE_API_KEY=

# AWS Bedrock (provider "bedrock", install with: pip install ".[bedrock]").
# Auth: either a Bedrock API key (bearer token, no AWS access keys) OR the AWS
# credential chain (env keys / ~/.aws/credentials / IAM role / AWS_PROFILE). Set
# the region either way; a bearer token takes precedence when both are present.
#AWS_BEARER_TOKEN_BEDROCK=
#AWS_DEFAULT_REGION=us-west-2
#AWS_PROFILE=

# Optional: point at a remote Ollama server. When unset, defaults to
# the local instance at http://localhost:11434/v1. Convention follows
# the broader Ollama ecosystem; both the CLI dropdown and programmatic
# client pick this up.
#OLLAMA_BASE_URL=http://your-ollama-host:11434/v1

# BTCUSDT AI Signal Pipeline — LLM selection (model comparison).
# Configuration-driven: switch providers/models without touching code.
# Supported model keys: deepseek-v4-flash | qwen3-8b | qwen3-4b
# DeepSeek needs DEEPSEEK_API_KEY (above); Ollama needs no key. Ollama's
# endpoint is OLLAMA_BASE_URL (above) or BTCUSDT_LLM_BASE_URL.
#BTCUSDT_LLM_PROVIDER=deepseek            # deepseek | ollama | openai_compatible
#BTCUSDT_LLM_MODEL=deepseek-v4-flash      # or qwen3-8b / qwen3-4b / any custom id
#BTCUSDT_LLM_BASE_URL=                    # optional endpoint override
#BTCUSDT_LLM_TIMEOUT=                     # optional request timeout (seconds)
#BTCUSDT_LLM_MAX_RETRIES=                 # optional SDK retry budget
#BTCUSDT_LLM_TEMPERATURE=                 # optional sampling temperature
#BTCUSDT_LLM_MAX_TOKENS=                  # optional output-token cap

# Phase 5 multi-agent analysis mode. "multi" runs the TradingAgents-style
# committee debate (analyst > bull > bear > trader > risk manager) against the
# SAME provider/model configured above (5 LLM calls per closed candle). Any
# other value or an unset variable keeps the single-call structured analysis.
# Precedence: Settings page (Web UI / database) > this env var > default single.
# The backtest benchmark is unaffected by this flag.
#BTCUSDT_ANALYSIS_MODE=single              # single | multi

# Optional: override DEFAULT_CONFIG without editing code.
# Any TRADINGAGENTS_* variable below, when set, replaces the matching key
# in tradingagents/default_config.py. Values are coerced to the type of
# the existing default (bool / int / str), so "true"/"3" work as expected.
# In the CLI, setting the LLM provider / models / backend URL / language
# also skips the matching interactive selection step (useful for
# OpenAI-compatible endpoints like opencode or LM Studio, and unattended runs).
#TRADINGAGENTS_LLM_PROVIDER=openai
#TRADINGAGENTS_DEEP_THINK_LLM=gpt-5.4
#TRADINGAGENTS_QUICK_THINK_LLM=gpt-5.4-mini
#TRADINGAGENTS_LLM_BACKEND_URL=
#TRADINGAGENTS_OUTPUT_LANGUAGE=English
#TRADINGAGENTS_MAX_DEBATE_ROUNDS=1
#TRADINGAGENTS_MAX_RISK_ROUNDS=1
#TRADINGAGENTS_CHECKPOINT_ENABLED=false
# Sampling temperature (lower = less run-to-run variation on models that
# honor it). Unset leaves each provider at its default. See the README
# "Reproducibility" note — no setting makes LLM output fully deterministic.
#TRADINGAGENTS_TEMPERATURE=0.0
# LLM SDK retry budget forwarded to every provider. Unset leaves each SDK at its
# own default (usually 2). Raise it to ride out bursty 429 rate-limit throttling
# on rate-limited deployments (e.g. Azure OpenAI) instead of aborting the run.
#TRADINGAGENTS_LLM_MAX_RETRIES=6
# Cap on output tokens forwarded to every provider (Gemini's max_output_tokens
# too). Unset leaves each provider at its default. Set it to bound a model that
# emits unbounded reasoning/output and hangs or trips a gateway idle timeout.
#TRADINGAGENTS_MAX_TOKENS=8192
# Provider-specific reasoning/thinking depth (optional; unset = provider
# default). Setting one also skips the matching interactive prompt.
#TRADINGAGENTS_OPENAI_REASONING_EFFORT=medium
#TRADINGAGENTS_GOOGLE_THINKING_LEVEL=high
#TRADINGAGENTS_ANTHROPIC_EFFORT=high

# BTCUSDT Telegram notifications (Phase 11) — read-only alert channel.
# Notices: new PENDING_ENTRY signal, position OPEN, TP/SL close (with demo PnL +
# balance), ambiguous candle. No commands are accepted; Telegram never controls
# trading. Disabled by default (zero network calls). NEVER commit a real token.
#BTCUSDT_TELEGRAM_ENABLED=false
#BTCUSDT_TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN=
#BTCUSDT_TELEGRAM_CHAT_ID=
#BTCUSDT_TELEGRAM_TIMEOUT=
#BTCUSDT_TELEGRAM_MAX_RETRIES=
#BTCUSDT_TELEGRAM_BACKOFF=

# BTCUSDT Web Dashboard + Settings (Phase 15) — stdlib HTTP dashboard.
# Serve the SPA + JSON API with:  python -m signal_engine web --host --port
# Purely read-only wrt trading state; Settings writes go through the
# ConfigService safety rules (apply-when-idle / demo lock while a signal is
# active). Host defaults to 127.0.0.1; bind to 0.0.0.0 only behind a firewall.
#BTCUSDT_WEB_HOST=127.0.0.1
#BTCUSDT_WEB_PORT=8000
# Location of the 0600 file storing the Settings-page secrets (AI provider API
# key, Telegram bot token). Never committed; never written to SQLite or logs.
#BTCUSDT_SECRETS_FILE=data/btcusdt_secrets.json

# BTCUSDT Production Runtime (Phase 14) — 24/7 daemon configuration.
# Overrides for the `python -m signal_engine` daemon and its CLI. All values
# are optional; the defaults below match the spec. NEVER place real trading
# credentials here — the demo never executes real Binance orders.
#BTCUSDT_SYMBOL=BTCUSDT                  # default market-data symbol (BTCUSDT/ETHUSDT/XAUUSDT)
#                                       # NOTE: the active symbol is normally chosen in the
#                                       # Settings page ("Active Symbol"). DB setting > this env
#                                       # > BTCUSDT. Exactly ONE symbol is analysed at a time.
#BTCUSDT_TIMEFRAME=1h                    # AI analysis timeframe (closed 1H candles)
#BTCUSDT_DB_PATH=                        # SQLite path (default: ./trading_agents.db)
#BTCUSDT_RUNTIME_SCHEDULER_POLL=30       # seconds between scheduler passes
#BTCUSDT_RUNTIME_MONITOR_POLL=15         # seconds between TP/SL monitor polls (1m candles)

# Demo account (AGENTS.md section 13). 20 USDT initial balance, 2 USDT margin,
# 10x leverage, 1% risk, 0.04% fee. Users may change these freely.
#BTCUSDT_DEMO_INITIAL_BALANCE=20
#BTCUSDT_DEMO_MARGIN_PER_TRADE=2
#BTCUSDT_DEMO_LEVERAGE=10
#BTCUSDT_DEMO_RISK_PERCENT=1
#BTCUSDT_DEMO_FEE_RATE=0.0004            # fraction (0.04%)

# ── Docker deployment (Dockerfile + docker-compose.yml) ──────────────────────
# The container runs BOTH the daemon and the web dashboard in one process
# (docker/entrypoint-signalengine.sh). On the server:
#   cp .env.example .env   # then edit the provider section below
#   docker compose up -d --build
#   # dashboard -> http://SERVER:8000
#
# The `btcusdt_data` volume maps to /app/data and persists the SQLite ledger
# plus the secrets file across rebuilds; restart recovery keeps an OPEN demo
# position intact (it is never re-analyzed).
#
# Choose ONE provider block (mutually exclusive):
#
# (1) Local Ollama already installed on the SERVER HOST (models pulled), NOT in
#     Docker. The host Ollama MUST listen on 0.0.0.0 so the container can reach
#     it via host.docker.internal (default binds 127.0.0.1):
#       export OLLAMA_HOST=0.0.0.0   # or configure the systemd service
#BTCUSDT_LLM_PROVIDER=ollama
#BTCUSDT_LLM_MODEL=qwen3:4b
#OLLAMA_BASE_URL=http://host.docker.internal:11434
#
# (2) OpenRouter (OpenAI-compatible API, no local model; load credits at
#     openrouter.ai). The free models (:free) are rate-limited; a paid route has
#     no quota besides your balance. A 1-hourly signal loop is a light load:
#BTCUSDT_LLM_PROVIDER=openrouter
#BTCUSDT_LLM_MODEL=google/gemma-4-31b-it:free   # or deepseek/deepseek-chat
#OPENROUTER_API_KEY=sk-or-xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx
#
# Container data paths (defaults are exported by the Dockerfile; only override
# to relocate them inside the mounted volume).
#BTCUSDT_DB_PATH=/app/data/btcusdt_signals.db
#BTCUSDT_SECRETS_FILE=/app/data/btcusdt_secrets.json
#
# API keys/bot tokens entered on the Dashboard Settings page are stored in
# $BTCUSDT_SECRETS_FILE inside the volume (0600). They persist across rebuilds
# and are never written to the database, logs, or git.
